    "For Ladnu weddings, the package decision is really a headcount decision first and a style decision second. Once we know how many people need styling — the groom, close family, and the wider baraat if applicable — we can recommend artist numbers and a realistic tying window. Families sometimes assume a bigger package is always safer, but an accurately sized package based on your actual guest list is usually more cost-effective and easier to schedule than an oversized one. If you're unsure of the final numbers this early, a rough range is enough to start the conversation; we'll confirm the exact count closer to the date. Multi-function weddings in Ladnu — where the same family books a haldi, sangeet and wedding day styling — often benefit from a combined package rather than three separate bookings, since it keeps pricing and artist scheduling consistent across all three events. If your celebration includes destination elements, such as a portion of the wedding happening outside Ladnu itself, mention that upfront too, since it changes how the package and travel logistics are structured.",
