  "bidar": [
    "Bidar sees weddings across a mix of settings — banquet halls, hotel lawns, rooftop venues and home courtyards — and each one changes how the tying schedule is planned. A hotel booking usually means a fixed preparation room and predictable access, while a home or courtyard function often needs the team to adapt around family rituals happening in parallel. We ask about the venue type early so the right number of artists and the right pace are set from the start, rather than guessing on the day. Peak wedding months in and around Bidar bring tighter artist availability, so dates during the busiest weeks benefit from earlier confirmation. Off-season and weekday bookings tend to have more flexibility on timing and can sometimes accommodate later confirmations. Either way, the core planning stays the same: confirm the property, the room being used for styling, and roughly how many people need to be ready before the first ritual or the baraat departure. Weather is a smaller factor for most Bidar bookings since safa tying happens indoors or under cover, but for any outdoor portrait session immediately after styling, we factor in extra time so fabric and finishing hold up under natural light.",
    "For Bidar weddings, the package decision is really a headcount decision first and a style decision second. Once we know how many people need styling — the groom, close family, and the wider baraat if applicable — we can recommend artist numbers and a realistic tying window. Families sometimes assume a bigger package is always safer, but an accurately sized package based on your actual guest list is usually more cost-effective and easier to schedule than an oversized one. If you're unsure of the final numbers this early, a rough range is enough to start the conversation; we'll confirm the exact count closer to the date. Multi-function weddings in Bidar — where the same family books a haldi, sangeet and wedding day styling — often benefit from a combined package rather than three separate bookings, since it keeps pricing and artist scheduling consistent across all three events. If your celebration includes destination elements, such as a portion of the wedding happening outside Bidar itself, mention that upfront too, since it changes how the package and travel logistics are structured.",
  ],
