    "Across Sonipat, wedding venues range from compact family halls to larger destination-style properties, and the safa tying plan changes with the scale of the venue. Smaller, more intimate functions usually need a shorter, tighter schedule with the groom styled first and the rest of the group following quickly after. Larger multi-hall or multi-day venues need a longer plan, sometimes spanning more than one function in the same property, and we treat each function as its own booking within the same visit. Local venues in Sonipat are generally easy to access, which keeps setup time short, but properties further from the main area may need an earlier arrival buffer. We recommend sharing the venue name and rough guest count as early as possible, even before the date is fully locked, so we can flag any availability concerns during peak wedding weeks. If the celebration includes more than one ceremony — a haldi, a sangeet, the main wedding — let us know all the dates together so the Sonipat team can plan artist availability across the full run rather than one date at a time.",
    "For Sonipat weddings, the package decision is really a headcount decision first and a style decision second. Once we know how many people need styling — the groom, close family, and the wider baraat if applicable — we can recommend artist numbers and a realistic tying window. Families sometimes assume a bigger package is always safer, but an accurately sized package based on your actual guest list is usually more cost-effective and easier to schedule than an oversized one. If you're unsure of the final numbers this early, a rough range is enough to start the conversation; we'll confirm the exact count closer to the date. Multi-function weddings in Sonipat — where the same family books a haldi, sangeet and wedding day styling — often benefit from a combined package rather than three separate bookings, since it keeps pricing and artist scheduling consistent across all three events. If your celebration includes destination elements, such as a portion of the wedding happening outside Sonipat itself, mention that upfront too, since it changes how the package and travel logistics are structured.",
